## Test Smell Audit — Academic Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` | **Framework:** MSTest 4.1 | **Calibration:** Integration (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell 1)

**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)  
**Rationale:** `if/else` changes which assertion runs — one branch is never exercised, hiding a gap.

```csharp
// ❌ Current
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Split into two deterministic tests or assert the known type explicitly:

```csharp
// ✅ Fixed — assert on the known scenario
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One branch may silently never execute in CI, providing false confidence.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell 4)

**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)  
**Rationale:** Exercises 100 inserts but asserts nothing. Passes even if every insert silently fails.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertion
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
```

**Fix:**

```csharp
// ✅ Fixed
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_AllRecordsPersisted()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False pass — 100% "coverage" with zero verified behavior.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test (Smell 3) *(downgraded from High — integration calibration)*

**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)  
**Rationale:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` introduces 3 seconds of dead wait and non-determinism.

```csharp
// ❌ Current
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix:** Use a polling/retry helper with a timeout:

```csharp
// ✅ Fixed — deterministic wait with timeout
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures under load; needlessly slow suite (3 s per run).

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Catalog)

**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)  
**Rationale:** 4 assertions, none with a message. A failure reports only a line number, not *which property* was wrong.

```csharp
// ❌ Current
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix:** Add discriminating messages:

```csharp
// ✅ Fixed
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage when CI fails — developer must read source to identify which property diverged.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The following tests are well-structured — clear arrange/act/assert, single concern, contextually obvious assertions:

| Method | Notes |
|--------|-------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clean AAA, focused on one mutation |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single assertion on absence — ideal |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count `3` is self-documenting (3 inserts immediately above) |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good concurrency scenario with clear verification |

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Rationale |
|----------|-------|-----------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~2 min | Prevents a silent false-pass — highest risk |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~5 min | Eliminates hidden dead branch |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~10 min | Removes flakiness + speeds suite by 3 s |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | ~3 min | Quality-of-life for failure triage |

**Overall verdict:** 4 of 8 tests are clean. The remaining 4 have addressable smells — none exotic, all fixable in under 30 minutes total. The suite is structurally sound but needs the above tightening to be fully trustworthy.
